@remotionco is a lightweight office on your desktop that helps the team connect through more casual &amp; social conversations.
As part of this, we also have a lightweight in-call experience.

Around I think is more focused on just that last bit.

@jamesclift @rallstadt I'm also unable to both at the same time, so I partition the day into thinking &amp; doing times.

My problem is then using the thinking time to "do" anyways.

To focus on the thinking, it helps me to aim to share a written artifact with the team by the end of the thinking block.

@stephsmithio @codiwork @NomadList @spatialxr @SlidesWith Re tools, I see 2 main categories:

*Event replacements* like happy hour apps are easy to roll out but have limited long-term impact

*Environment upgrades* to encourage collaboration &amp; relationship building are hard to adopt but transform the team

